A||N||7||count_iblis||To rice or not to rice that is the question||||1||
Z||000000||count_iblis||10-20-2000||02:37 AM||||Hey all, Im not a ricer or anything but i do have a 6 cyl probe gt.  Well I sortta went the way of a the rice.  I put on a HKS Supra Dragger on the car to replace to orig. exhaust.  I love the way it sounds, sounds like a indy car!  I also kinda like some of the bolt ons also that the ricers use.  Now i seen a post before on here like if i put quad 4 stickers on my car will i be considered a ricer?  I guess what im trying to get at is, although im not a punk ricer i do like some of the stuff out there for the sports compact car.  so if any of you ever see me at a gathering please dont look and then just smirk off ok?  <P>Count<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-20-2000||08:19 AM||||I worked at NOPI for nearly 2 years... and Had a 94 300TT, while i was there. just an example.. my car.. NO stickers unless the company GAVE me somthing, NOT a discount.. ANYONE can get a discount. Don't advertise for stuff you had to pay for! don't put Neuspeed stickers on your car.. Neuspeed doesn't make anything to fit your car.. HKS is a GREAT company.. with amazing customer service and very a impressive product line. your question too rice... is relative.. do you have wheels that stick out? stickers all over for stuff you paid for and for stuff that doesn't fit your car? lots of vinyl all over it? and in the event you DO lose a race will you not stop and chat with whom ever you fell to but instead you "fly by" with only your exhaust note to back you up! For $585 that the HKS retails for I'd be hard pressed to not want to show off what i had. the Probe although not really tuner friendly they are quick and fun to drive. hope that helps answer your quandry. <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||10-20-2000||11:37 AM||||besides the "feral" winshield graphic i've always had on the car i want to take off everything else, even the original pontiac and fiero labels. personal prefrence. i do at the moment have 1 sticker. some up and coming band named hybrid. with ford, camaro, kawasaki, and soon fiero gt parts on my '87 coupe, it seemed appropriate. it's on an unpainted wing though so i'll eventually lose it too. <P>do what you like. at the next show your car will be one of the more interesting one to me if i'm there. i already know what a stock fiero looks like.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)||||reg||1
Z||000003||contra||10-21-2000||08:51 AM||||my understanding is<BR>you're not rice if you're actually gaining performance out of the addons you bolt on. If you're hindering your car, or just adding things for looks or sounds, then forget about it, it's a rice thing to do. I've seen some crazy things all the way to plastic fake intercoolers, to an electronic Blow off valve soundeffect box (to make you sound like you have a mean turbo!) what will these peepz think of next? Electronic sounding v12 exhaust?<BR>I myself am looking into buying a Mitsubishi Eclipse GSX AWD next year, and i want to mod the hell out of it. Mind you, i will be doing all performance stuff, nothing for looks except maybe tinted windows, blue headlights, and rims. The rest will be straight pipe, bigger turbo and BOV, as well as ram air etc.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Xtreme Fiero's||10-21-2000||02:08 PM|||| Ram Air? on a TURBO ECLIPSE!!! with an intercooler? WHY WHY WHY.....<P><BR> (Just a confused Ricer here) <P>1FST2M6: (DROOL... VG30DE-TT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> DROOL...) ||||reg||1
